Z||000000||SloPonti||01-14-2000||07:02 PM||||This sensor is for a 84 pontiac fiero and it goes into the head buy the thermostat and it is on the back/exhaust manifold side of the head! the part i have now is broken and i need to replace it for my new motor! i think it is the fan switch but can someone tell me for sure!<BR>thanks <P>click below to see picture <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/part.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/sloponti/part.jpg</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||01-14-2000||09:26 PM||||Looks like coolant temp, bring it to the parts store to match it up. Ask for a fan switch and a coolant temp sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||01-14-2000||10:18 PM||||I believe that is the coolant temp switch.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shipbuilder||01-14-2000||10:27 PM||||On my 84 the horizontal sensor that screws into the front of the head is for the fan. The vertical one right above it is for the temp guage and indicator light. To remove any doubt as to what it does, just hook a jumper from the wire that goes to the sensor to ground. With the ignition switch turned on either the fan will start, the temp. guage will peg or the indicator light will come on. Then you will know exactly what the sensor is for.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SloPonti||01-16-2000||06:35 PM||||i took it to the parts store and they are telling me it a dealer only item but they can't exactly tell me what it is? does anyone know for sure what it is!<BR>thanks<BR>rob||||reg||1
Z||000005||William Federle||01-16-2000||08:17 PM||||The Fiero store has a fan switch for a 1984 Fiero without A/C for $14.95 and one for the same car with A/C for $39.95<P>I usually buy parts for my 1984 Fiero at Advance Auto (they use to be Parts America) and before that Western Auto. Their prices are usually about 1/2 what the Fiero store charges - but the Fiero store has some items that Advance Auto doesn't. <P>By the way your new engine looks great.<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 01-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shipbuilder||01-16-2000||09:57 PM||||I purchased the fan sensor about six months ago at Advance Auto Parts for about $7.00. They had all three coolant sensors on the shelf.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||01-16-2000||11:24 PM||||try wrenchead.com they list nearly everything. As I recall the sendor in the thermostat neck is the ECM coolant sender. the one in the head is the light/gauge sender if it has 2 contacts. did it have green wires? those are the light/gauge wires.||||reg||1
